00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.546
And we don't know what's going to happen

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.347
with the grand jury,

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.449
but we should keep in mind

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.084
that Michael Cohen

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.386
was charged and convicted

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.989
and was guilty in connection

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:56.523
with the payoffs

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.557
to Stormy Daniels

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.192
on behalf of individual No.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:00:59.559
One.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.262
Well, that means that it's highly unusual

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.263
for individual No.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.865
One, not also to be indicted.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:09.035
So expect that to happen sometime soon.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.170
I will play out.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.671
I'm not sure

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.505
I didn't

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.573
stick with you for one more,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.241
Richard, as we look at all of this

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.409
and everybody's trying to read

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.410
the tea leaves here, right.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.578
Trying to figure out

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.813
what's going to happen.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:20.146
Part of

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.214
that is because of what

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:21.915
the former president

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.149
put out over the weekend

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.851
saying that this was going to happen,

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.953
as Paula said, his own attorneys

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.455
refuting that

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.289
But the fact that

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.958
this narrative is now out there,

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:33.827
what does that do?

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.728
How does that weigh on prosecutors

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.496
at this point?

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.431
How does that inform any decisions

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.101
if at all, knowing what could be coming

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.602
in terms of a reaction?

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.405
The Donald Trump is

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.006
going to try to play this

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:51.811
to rev up his base and cause unrest.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.146
But the prosecutors

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.447
should continue to do their job.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.649
That's what prosecutors are there for.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.885
The problem is that the much more serious

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.353
charges are in their hands,

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.388
that the Department of Justice,

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.891
the charges for sedition and insurrection

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.359
in connection with the events

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.528
after the 2020 election.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:11.164
And unfortunately, we have a situation

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.132
where the

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.433
district attorneys,

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.400
both in New York

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.401
and in Fulton County,

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.370
Georgia, are far ahead

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.638
of the Department of Justice,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.973
or at least appear to be far ahead

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.307
of the Department of Justice

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.575
in their investigations.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.943
Empanel and grand jury

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.479
and moving toward indictments

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.781
without DOJ having taken action

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.116
