00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:30.817
The sedition

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.484
and insurrection

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.852
charges would disqualify

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.621
Donald Trump from public office.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.723
Under the 14th Amendment, Section three.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.291
Those really should be

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.826
the first charges to be brought.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.994
They should have been brought

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.128
a long time ago.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.163
It's been over two years

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.465
since the insurrection on January six.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.300
And unfortunately, without air

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.301
support from the

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.070
Department of Justice,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.372
the district attorneys

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.373
are going to be subjected

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:57.243
to very vicious attacks from Donald Trump

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.012
and his supporters,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.547
which I believe could feed into

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:01.915
more civil unrest.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:02.882
It's a very,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.185
very precarious situation right now.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.252
Jonathan,

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.520
I want to bring you into this discussion,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.422
because talk about unprecedented here,

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.557
the possibility and again,

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.658
we don't know if it's going to happen,

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.660
but the possibility of a former president

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.894
being arrested raises

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:18.765
all kinds of security concerns

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.533
and processes we just never seen before.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:20.833
Yes.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.067
You know,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.135
Trump called for protests

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:22.569
over the weekend.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:22.936
There's that

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.171
and I'm sure the security concerns there.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.940
What should we be looking for

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.608
and how will this even work?

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.677
Which different agencies from the state,

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.311
from the city,

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.245
from the federal government

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.080
might be involved with this? Yeah,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.849
John, great question.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.251
And listen, there's a lot of uncertainty.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.419
We don't have a line of sight

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.520
of exactly

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.122
what the prosecutors are doing right now.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.791
But we do have a line of sight of what

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.892
law enforcement is doing.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:46.993
And what they're doing

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:47.760
is, you know,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.262
with the backdrop of actions

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.164
from January six,

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.066
they're being hyper coordinated

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.901
around their efforts

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.035
and those efforts are across

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.537
multiple law enforcement

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.472
entities, both at the state, local

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.773
and federal level.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.574
But what's really interesting,

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.475
John, is that the roles

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.277
and responsibilities

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.612
around all of the different law

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.814
enforcement entities that are involved

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.881
are different.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.183
They have a different remit

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.618
on how they're addressing this issue.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.853
Let me just quickly walk you through

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.054
what we're what we're looking

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.656
at, the NYPD, right.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.757
They are

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.759
in charge of maintaining civil order.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.927
So what they're going to do

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.028
is they're going to be focused

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.463
on the area around the courthouse.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.765
But also New York City at large. Right.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:26.899
There are multiple areas

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.769
where protests could could spark

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.737
at a moment's notice.

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.673
And remember, NYPD has a dual role here.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.608
Protests are individuals.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.609
Protesters are individuals

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:37.410
who are exercising

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.778
their First Amendment rights

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.413
and they need to be protected

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.582
in the execution of those rights.

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:45.018
But NYPD is also keenly aware

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.420
of any type of violent activity

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.423
that may stem from these protests.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.058
So they have a dual remit there

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:53.526
on maintaining that civil order

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:54.894
and protecting protesters.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:55.228
New York

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.296
state court officers,

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.330
they are the ones that are

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.132
going to be protecting the courthouse,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.567
the physical building itself, again,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.069
from any type of activity.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.937
The FBI there involved. Why?

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.272
Because they're monitoring

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:06.906
for any types

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.775
of violations of federal law

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:10.643
by any of these protesters.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.544
They're looking for acts

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.812
of potential domestic

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.047
violence by extremists.

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.181
So they're involved.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.616
Now, you have the Secret Service,

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:17.216
the Secret Service

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.718
playing an interesting role.

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.320
Usually we see the Secret Service

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.587
as a coordinating entity.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.689
They're the ones that usually

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:23.122
come up

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.191
with these security plans for rallies and

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:26.392
speeches in

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.394
any type of political events surrounding,

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:28.628
you know,

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:30.463
either a sitting or former president.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.598
But in this case, they're not

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.634
they are in a protective mode.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.235
They are viewing this

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.304
as really an administrative movement

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.473
where they have to protect Donald Trump

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.709
from point a to point B,

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:44.310
let him do his business

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.978
before the court and leave.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.880
They are not playing that active role

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.549
that we typically see them in.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.317
They're not providing the magnetometers

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.952
at the at the courthouse.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:53.853
They're not providing

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.887
the perimeter security

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.155
that we typically see.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:56.923
Now, are they

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:57.623
are they working

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:58.858
with law enforcement partners?

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.059
The answer is yes.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.561
They're going to be informed.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.129
But they are not the controlling entity,

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.030
which is something rare

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.398
that we typically don't see

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.033
the Secret Service engage with.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.968
Jonathan, real quickly,

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.536
how much, if at all,

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.171
have the events of January six?

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:15.108
What we saw unfold there influenced

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.176
the preparations that are likely

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.311
underway at this point?

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:23.383
This is they're heavily weighted.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:23.649
Right.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.084
And I think that you've seen

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.486
from January six

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:26.986
across

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:27.620
a whole

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.223
variety of different types of events

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.792
Neal, both in New York, Washington, D.C.,

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.093
but across the nation,

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.795
law enforcement is is heavily

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.964
reliant upon information sharing,

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:40.032
intelligence and preparedness

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.467
they have to be

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.301
they have to plan

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.203
for every type of eventuality,

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:44.504
you know,

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.705
especially in a city

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.240
like New York, where, you know,

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.841
there are multiple locations

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.377
where in incidents could occur,

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.913
sparked by and fueled by,

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:54.280
